---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'September 25, 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy - ScoreSpace"
  description="How ScoreSpace, Inc. handles information in the games we publish on Apple Messages, YouTube Playables, Discord, Reddit, and the web."
>
  <section class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <div class="container legal">
      <p>
        This policy explains how <strong>ScoreSpace, Inc.</strong> ("ScoreSpace," "we," "us," or
        "our") handles information in connection with the games we publish (the "Games") on
        Apple's Messages app, YouTube Playables, Discord, Reddit, and the web, including on our
        own domains and on itch.io.
      </p>
      <p>
        By playing the Games you agree to this policy. If you do not agree, please do not play.
        Questions go to <a href="mailto:legal@scorespace.net">legal@scorespace.net</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>1. How the Games are built</h2>
      <p>
        The Games run in different ways on different platforms, and that changes what we can see.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          On <strong>Apple Messages, Discord, and the web</strong>, the Games talk to servers we
          run on Cloudflare and report usage to PostHog, our analytics provider. Sections 2 and 3
          describe what those Games collect.
        </li>
        <li>
          On <strong>YouTube Playables and Reddit</strong>, the Games run entirely inside those
          platforms and send nothing to us. Section 4 describes what each platform does.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>2. Information we collect</h2>
      <p>This section applies to the Games on Apple Messages, Discord, and the web.</p>
      <p>
        <strong>Identifiers.</strong> On first launch each Game generates a random identifier and
        stores it on your device or in your browser's storage. It is not your device identifier,
        not an advertising identifier, and is not derived from any hardware or account
        identifier. Deleting the Game, or clearing the site's data in your browser, deletes it;
        starting again produces a new identifier that cannot be linked to the previous one. Where
        a platform gives us an identifier of its own, section 4 says so.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Network information.</strong> Your IP address, received when the Game contacts
        our servers.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Technical information.</strong> Device model and type, operating system or
        browser and version, language, time zone, screen and window size, and timestamps.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Usage and gameplay information.</strong> Which Game and mode you play, screens you
        open, moves you make, games started, completed and abandoned, wins, losses and draws,
        invitations sent and accepted, features used, and errors and crashes. We also keep running
        totals for an installation, such as sessions, games played, win rate and streaks, so we
        can distinguish new players from returning ones.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Game state.</strong> When you play with someone else, the state of the game in
        progress is stored on our servers so that every player's device can share it. Games played
        on your own are handled on your device.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>A display name</strong> of up to 14 characters, on platforms that let you enter
        one, if you choose to.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Group context.</strong> So that we can understand how many games a group produces,
        usage records carry a key for the group you are playing in. On Apple Messages this is an
        anonymous value derived from the conversation; it cannot be reversed into the conversation
        or a participant, and it is not the conversation's own identifier. On Discord it is the
        server and channel identifier.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Information we do not collect</h2>
      <p>
        The Games never transmit the contents of the puzzles themselves: answers, solutions,
        words, letters or guesses. We do not receive your password, contacts, photos, location, or
        the contents of your messages.
      </p>
      <p>
        The Games contain no advertising SDK of our own. We do not track you across other
        companies' apps or websites, and the Games therefore do not request App Tracking
        Transparency permission. Play currencies in the Games, such as chips, have no monetary
        value, cannot be sold, transferred or redeemed, and no real money is wagered at any point.
        Where a platform lets you make a purchase in a Game, that platform processes it; section 4
        explains what we receive.
      </p>

      <h2>4. What each platform gives us, and what it keeps</h2>

      <h3>4.1 Apple Messages (iMessage)</h3>
      <p>
        An iMessage app is not a conventional app. Apple provides the Games with an anonymous,
        per-app identifier for each participant in a conversation, a random value that has no
        meaning outside that Game, and provides no way to request anything further. We do not
        receive your name, phone number, email address, Apple ID, contacts, photos or location,
        and we never receive the contents of your messages. Where a Game displays a player name,
        it is a name that player typed into the Game themselves. The Games on Apple Messages
        contain no advertising and no in-app purchases. Apple distributes the Games and operates
        the Messages platform under its own
        <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h3>4.2 YouTube Playables</h3>
      <p>
        On YouTube the Games run inside the YouTube app or website. YouTube's rules do not allow a
        Playable to contact any server other than Google's or YouTube's, so these Games make no
        calls to our servers or to anyone else's, and never ask you for a name or any other
        personal information. YouTube tells the Game only your language setting. Your progress is
        saved by YouTube against your YouTube account, scores are sent to YouTube for its own
        features, any advertising shown around or inside a Game is served and controlled by
        YouTube, and errors are logged to YouTube. We receive no information about you from
        YouTube. YouTube's handling of this information is governed by the
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h3>4.3 Discord</h3>
      <p>
        On Discord the Games run as Activities inside Discord. When you authorize an Activity,
        Discord provides us with your Discord user ID, username and display name, avatar, and the
        identifiers of the server and channel where the Activity was opened. We use these to seat
        players at the same table, show names and avatars to the other players, and group games by
        channel. Everything in sections 2 and 3 also applies. Some Games offer purchases through
        Discord's store; Discord processes the payment and we receive only an entitlement record:
        what was bought, when, and by which user ID. We never receive payment card or billing
        details. Discord's own practices are described in the
        <a href="https://discord.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Discord Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h3>4.4 Reddit</h3>
      <p>
        On Reddit the Games run on Reddit's Developer Platform, on Reddit's servers. Reddit provides
        the Game with your Reddit user ID and username, and the subreddit and post you are playing
        in. Game data is stored within Reddit's Developer Platform and is not sent to our servers or
        to our analytics provider. Some Games offer purchases through Reddit; Reddit processes the
        payment and we do not receive your payment details. Reddit's own practices are described in
        the
        <a href="https://www.reddit.com/policies/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Reddit Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h3>4.5 Web (our domains and itch.io)</h3>
      <p>
        On the web the Games run in your browser, either on a domain we operate or embedded on
        itch.io. There is no account and no sign-in. The random identifier described in section 2
        lives in your browser's storage, and clearing the site's data removes it. Everything in
        sections 2 and 3 applies. When you play on itch.io, itch.io serves the page and may collect
        its own information under the
        <a href="https://itch.io/docs/legal/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">itch.io Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>5. How we use this information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To operate the Games, and in particular to keep a shared game synchronised between players' devices.</li>
        <li>To understand how the Games are used, so that we can improve them.</li>
        <li>To diagnose errors and crashes.</li>
        <li>To detect fraud, abuse and cheating, and to enforce our Terms.</li>
        <li>To deliver purchases you make through Discord or Reddit.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Where the law of your country requires a legal basis, we rely on the need to perform our
        agreement with you (to run the Game and deliver purchases), our legitimate interests (to
        improve the Games, keep them secure and prevent cheating), and your consent where a
        platform or the law requires it.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not use this information for advertising, we do not build advertising profiles, and
        we do not sell or rent it.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Who else receives it</h2>
      <p>For the Games on Apple Messages, Discord, and the web:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>PostHog</strong>, for product analytics.
          <a href="https://posthog.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Privacy policy</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Cloudflare</strong>, our hosting and network provider.
          <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Privacy policy</a>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Each is bound by agreement to process this information only on our instructions and to
        protect it to at least the standard set out in this policy. We do not authorise them to use
        it for their own purposes, and we add no other third-party service to the Games.
      </p>
      <p>
        The platforms that distribute the Games (Apple, Google and YouTube, Discord, Reddit, and
        itch.io) receive information directly from you and from the Game as described in section 4,
        under their own privacy policies, and we do not control what they collect.
      </p>
      <p>
        We may also disclose information when required by law, or to protect the rights, safety and
        property of ScoreSpace, our players or the public, and in connection with a merger,
        acquisition, financing or sale of assets, in which case this policy continues to apply to
        it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our analytics and server infrastructure operate in the United States and on Cloudflare's
        global network, so information described here is processed outside your country, including
        in the United States. Where required, such transfers rely on the European Commission's
        Standard Contractual Clauses or an equivalent safeguard.
      </p>

      <h2>7. How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        Game state is retained while a game remains available to play or to look back on. Usage
        information is retained according to our analytics provider's retention period and is
        deleted when that period elapses. Purchase records are kept for as long as needed to honour
        the purchase and to meet our legal and accounting obligations. Information stored on your
        device or in your browser remains there until you delete the Game or clear the site's data.
        Information held by YouTube or Reddit is kept according to their own policies.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Your choices and your rights</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Stopping collection.</strong> You can stop all collection by deleting the Game
        from your device or clearing the site's data in your browser. This also removes the
        identifier described in section 2, together with your settings, profile and any game in
        progress held on the device. On Discord you can additionally remove the Activity's
        authorization in your Discord settings.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Deletion, access and other rights.</strong> To request deletion of information held
        on our servers, or to ask what we hold, contact
        <a href="mailto:legal@scorespace.net">legal@scorespace.net</a>, telling us which platform
        you played on, approximately when, and, for Discord or Reddit, your username there.
        Depending on where you live you may also have the right to access, correct, export,
        restrict or object to our use of your information, and to withdraw consent. Residents of
        the EEA and UK (under the GDPR) and of California (under the CCPA/CPRA) may have additional
        rights, including the right not to be discriminated against for exercising them. We do not
        sell or share personal information as those terms are defined under the CCPA/CPRA. We
        respond within 30 days and may need to verify your identity first. You may also complain to
        your local data protection authority.
      </p>
      <p>
        For information held by a platform rather than by us, such as your YouTube saves or your
        Reddit account, use that platform's own tools and privacy contacts.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Children</h2>
      <p>
        The Games are not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal
        information from children under 13. The platforms we publish on require users to be at
        least 13, and older in some jurisdictions. If you believe a child has provided us with
        personal information, contact
        <a href="mailto:legal@scorespace.net">legal@scorespace.net</a> and we will delete it.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Security</h2>
      <p>
        Everything the Games transmit travels over HTTPS, and access to our analytics and server
        infrastructure is restricted to those who need it. No method of transmission or storage is
        completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy from time to time. When we do, we will revise the "Last updated"
        date above. Your continued use of the Games after changes take effect constitutes
        acceptance of the revised policy.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Contact us</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy or our data practices:
        <a href="mailto:legal@scorespace.net">legal@scorespace.net</a>.
      </p>

      <p class="legal-footer-note">
        See also our <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}terms/`}>Terms &amp; Conditions</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .page-header {
    padding: 4rem 0 3rem;
    text-align: center;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--color-bg-secondary) 0%, var(--color-bg) 100%);
  }

  .page-header h1 {
    font-size: 3rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    color: white;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .subtitle {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .legal-section {
    padding: 3rem 0 5rem;
  }

  .legal {
    max-width: 780px;
  }

  .legal p {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .legal strong {
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .legal h2 {
    color: white;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }

  .legal h3 {
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    margin: 1.75rem 0 0.75rem;
  }

  .legal ul {
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem 1.25rem;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .legal li {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }

  .legal a {
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .legal a:hover {
    color: var(--color-accent-hover);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .legal-footer-note {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .page-header h1 {
      font-size: 2.25rem;
    }
  }
</style>
